; equality_length_mismatch_beats_the_charge: EQUALITY compares its vec
; lengths before it charges the expansion, so a mismatch is reported even
; when the budget could not pay.
;
; spec/xqvm/METERING.md ("Known Slack") places the length validation
; above the point where the expansion is charged: the handler reads its
; vecs "in order to validate vector lengths and compute the model growth
; the expansion will require". The model and the three VECPUSHes spend the
; budget of 64 bytes exactly, so charging first would raise
; MemoryLimitExceeded. equality_length_mismatch_beats_model_type pins the
; same comparison against the model register's type.

PUSH 2
BQMX r0          ; 16 bytes
VECI r1
PUSH 0
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r1       ; indices = [0, 1]
VECI r2
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2       ; coeffs = [1]; 64 bytes: the whole budget
PUSH 1           ; target
PUSH 1           ; penalty
EQUALITY r0 r1 r2
HALT
